{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Python Script Compilation Cache.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Python Script Compilation Cache.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender python script compilation cache blender python script compilation cache","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Python Script Compilation Cache.md","fileName":"Blender Python Script Compilation Cache.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Python Script Compilation Cache","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:20\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Embedded Python Internals]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Embedded Python Internals","Blender Python Execution API","Blender Python Script Execution","coreblenderdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Python Script Compilation Cache.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Python Script Compilation Cache.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender python script compilation cache blender python script compilation cache","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Python Script Compilation Cache.md","fileName":"Blender Python Script Compilation Cache.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Python Script Compilation Cache","heading":"Blender Python Script Compilation Cache","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Before Blender evaluates an uncompiled Text datablock, it can ask CPython to compile the source into bytecode and store the resulting object with that text. Later executions can reuse the compiled representation instead of repeating the parsing and compilation step.\n\nThe cache belongs to the internal [[Blender Python Execution API]] path and remains tied to the datablock being executed. It explains how [[Blender Python Script Execution]] can preserve an interactive author